  title "Qanguhu's Forty-Eighth Amendment"
  summary "Promenade Hei, a penguin colony, faces cascading crises as corruption spreads through its lower terraces while bureaucratic amendments to the Long-dark Edict create contradictions that worsen conditions. Wishai qingnu'Crest and other administrators attempt to manage dwindling fire-core supplies and spreading corruption through increasingly complex amendments, but each solution creates new problems—rationing formulas that incentivize migration to corrupted areas, cleansing protocols requiring non-existent resources, and labor policies that accelerate the spread of corruption by assigning Touched residents to the worst zones. As the colony spirals toward collapse despite maintaining its official \"thriving\" designation, the ancient sea creature Grandmother Deep observes from below, recognizing the system as a self-perpetuating cycle of disaster that the penguins document but cannot escape."
